          "title": "You'll want to know: انهار",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "انهار — inhāra — \"to collapse\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "انهار البيت القديم بعد المطر. inhāra al-bayt al-qadīm baʿda al-maṭar. The old house collapsed after the rain."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Present: ينهار, yanhār."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Of a person: انهار (inhāra) بعد الخبر, he broke down at the news."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "انهار (inhāra) is built on the native Arabic root h-w-r (Lane), said of a building or a bank of earth that falls down. It is Form VII, \"to tumble down\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
